After the sort=name;DROP... incident, a teammate proposes this fix for GET /v1/courses (PostgreSQL, node-postgres):

const sort = String(req.query.sort ?? "published_at");
const { rows } = await pool.query(
  "SELECT id, title, published_at FROM courses ORDER BY $1 DESC LIMIT 20",
  [sort]
);

The pull request says: "The value is now a bound parameter, so this is safe and still sorts by whatever column the client asks for."

Statement: "With this change, GET /v1/courses?sort=title returns the courses sorted by their title."
